WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.582
Digital artifacts feel concrete, but they still need context.

00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:07.837
A screenshot, log excerpt, alert, file name, message header, ticket note,

00:00:07.837 --> 00:00:10.932
or threat intelligence indicator may be useful evidence,

00:00:10.932 --> 00:00:14.801
yet each one is also a representation of something else.

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:18.283
It may be filtered, cropped, transformed, copied, exported, summarized,

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:20.217
or separated from surrounding events.

00:00:20.217 --> 00:00:25.246
Counter-deception asks how the artifact was collected and what it can actually prove.

00:00:25.246 --> 00:00:27.181
Provenance should be captured early.

00:00:27.181 --> 00:00:31.436
Analysts should record the source system, collector, collection time, time range,

00:00:31.436 --> 00:00:34.531
query or view used, and any transformation applied.

00:00:34.531 --> 00:00:39.947
Timestamps deserve special care because systems may use local time, UTC, different time zones,

00:00:39.947 --> 00:00:43.816
clock drift, ingestion delay, or display formatting that hides precision.

00:00:43.816 --> 00:00:50.006
A timeline built from mixed sources should explain those differences before drawing a conclusion from sequence.

00:00:50.006 --> 00:00:53.101
Screenshots and logs are common sources of confusion.

00:00:53.101 --> 00:00:58.130
A screenshot can preserve useful visual context, but it can omit browser state,

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:02.772
account context, surrounding messages, or later changes in the system of record.

00:01:02.772 --> 00:01:06.641
A log line can confirm that an event was recorded,

00:01:06.641 --> 00:01:10.510
but it may not explain intent, user identity, session ownership,

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.991
or whether related events were excluded by the query.

00:01:13.991 --> 00:01:17.473
The artifact supports only the claim it actually supports.

00:01:17.473 --> 00:01:20.568
Where possible, corroborate with independent telemetry or records.

00:01:20.568 --> 00:01:25.210
A suspicious account change might be checked against identity logs, approval tickets,

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.145
device telemetry, and administrator actions.

00:01:27.145 --> 00:01:31.013
A claimed external indicator might be checked against original reporting,

00:01:31.013 --> 00:01:33.335
internal observations, and relevant time windows.

00:01:33.335 --> 00:01:37.977
Preserve evidence before drawing conclusions, maintain chain of custody for sensitive material,

00:01:37.977 --> 00:01:39.524
and document uncertainty plainly.

00:01:39.524 --> 00:01:43.780
Verification is strongest when artifact, context, and decision are tied together.
